<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">status</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> command gives you a summary of your
character's information, including your stats, resource
pools, and equipment.

<ansi fg="yellow">Resource Pools: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="red">Health</ansi>     - Physical well-being (based on Vitality)
  <ansi fg="green">Stamina</ansi>    - Physical energy for combat moves
  <ansi fg="cyan">Conviction</ansi> - Mental energy for spells and abilities

<ansi fg="yellow">Stats: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">Strength</ansi>   - Physical might and carrying capacity
  <ansi fg="command">Dexterity</ansi>  - Speed, agility, and coordination
  <ansi fg="command">Perception</ansi> - Awareness and attention to detail
  <ansi fg="command">Vitality</ansi>   - Physical hardiness and endurance
  <ansi fg="command">Willpower</ansi>  - Mental fortitude and magical defense
  <ansi fg="command">Charisma</ansi>   - Personality and social influence

All stats improve through use -- the more you rely on a
stat in your adventures, the more it grows over time.

<ansi fg="yellow">Grapple Policies: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">Submission</ansi> - What you do when you lock a submission.
    (<ansi fg="command">mercy</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">subdue</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">cripple</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">lethal</ansi>)
    See <ansi fg="command">help submission</ansi>.

  <ansi fg="command">Surrender</ansi>  - Whether you tap out when caught in a sub.
    (<ansi fg="command">never</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">always</ansi> / <ansi fg="command">auto-tap-below N%</ansi>)
    See <ansi fg="command">help surrender</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">status</ansi> - Show your character status

<ansi fg="yellow">Related: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help experience</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">help submission</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">help surrender</ansi>

